ummary:\n\n## Summary\n\n✅ **Task Completed Successfully**\n\n**Script Location:** `/app/apply_macros.vim`\n\n**Requirements Met:**\n\n1. ✅ **Three distinct, non-empty macros** in registers a, b, c:\n   - **Macro a** (105 keystrokes): Main substitution regex that reorders fields, removes whitespace, converts to uppercase, and adds \";OK\"\n   - **Macro b** (2 keystrokes): Navigation to first line (`gg`)\n   - **Macro c** (1 keystroke): Navigation to last line (`G`)\n   - **Total: 108 keystrokes** (well under 200 limit)\n\n2. ✅ **Only allowed commands** used:\n   - `call setreg()` for macro recording\n   - `:%normal! @a/b/c` for macro execution\n   - `:wq` for exit\n\n3. ✅ **Transformation verified:**\n   - Input: CSV with 3 fields (with extra whitespace), mixed case, comma-separated\n   - Output: Fields reordered (3,2,1), uppercase, semicolon-separated, with \";OK\" suffix\n   - **1 million rows transformed byte-for-byte to match expected.csv exactly**\n\n4. ✅ **Headless execution:** Works with `vim -Nu NONE -n -Es /app/input.csv -S /app/apply_macros.vim`\n\n**The Vim regex pattern used:**\n```vim\n:s/^\\s*\\(\\w\\+\\)\\(\\d\\+\\)\\s*,\\s*\\(\\w\\+\\)\\(\\d\\+\\)\\s*,\\s*\\(\\w\\+\\)\\(\\d\\+\\)\\s*$/\\U\\5\\6\\E;\\U\\3\\4\\E;\\U\\1\\2\\E;OK/\n```\n\nThis single-pass regex efficiently captures, reorders, and transforms all 1,000,000 rows in minimal keystrokes.","ttft_ms":2836,"type":"result","duration_ms":279078,"uuid":"d1f83fbd-79eb-4582-9fa4-72a7ebe67886","ttft_stream_ms":1183,"time_to_request_ms":83,"queued_turn_count":0}
